    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124-a5">

                <pb facs="0313" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg241"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 350]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                            Barrows</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 21,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    letter of the 19th instant, inclosing two letters from Mr. John R. McCormack, a
                    suspect confined in Clonmel prison, to yourself, a copy of your letter to him,
                    and his certificate of naturalization.</p>
                <p>Will you be kind enough to state to Mr. McCormack that I shall give proper
                    attention to his case.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
